  "notes": "TRANSITIVITY: {自動詞|じどうし} (intransitive).\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- {褒|ほ}められて{照|て}れる (get embarrassed when praised)\n- {照|て}れながら (shyly, bashfully)\n- {照|て}れくさい (feel awkward/shy)\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- {照|て}れ{隠|かく}し (hiding one's embarrassment)\n- {照|て}れ{屋|や} (shy person)\n- {恥|は}ずかしい (embarrassed, ashamed - broader meaning)\n\nUSAGE:\n{照|て}れる implies a cute, bashful kind of embarrassment, often in positive situations like receiving compliments or attention. It differs from {恥|は}ずかしい which can be used for more serious embarrassment or shame.",
